    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0528" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">FileNo.832.85/51a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-03T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 3, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In connection with the French negotiations for Brazilian ships, President, after
                    reading your telegrams, suggested to Secretary yesterday that this Government
                    had better stand aside and let French complete negotiations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
